==Translingual==

DOM, Design Original Manufacture, is a brand new business model that a factory or manufacturer owns key or patented technologies, which are used to manufacture products that are branded by the buyers. See [[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DOM_Business_Model|DOM Business Model]]

In the past, Chinese factories produce items that are designed and branded by foreigners, where the item of OEM ([[https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/OEM|Original Equipment Manufacturer]]) comes from. OEMs rely on their ability to drive down the cost of production through economies of scale. 

With the development of Chinese industries, China own many core technologies to create brand new products in the emerging industries such as electronic cigarettes, mobile phones and more. In these industries, Chinese factories have not only their own designs, but also core patents. In this case, Chinese factories occupy a new division of industry chain value. A brand new win-win busienss model is created . This is the new business model - DOM (Design Original Manufacturer).

